The number one reason trainees fail their fat loss goals is not an ineffective diet plan, but unrealistic timeline expectations. Commercial marketing promises dramatic 30-day transformations. In reality, healthy fat loss requires consistent, measured pacing. When trainees expect a steady drop on the scale every morning and inevitably hit natural water retention plateaus, they assume the diet has failed and quit.

