A landmark study by Phillips and Paddon-Jones demonstrated that resistance-trained athletes placed in a 40% caloric deficit who consumed 2.4 g/kg protein retained significantly more lean muscle mass and actually gained small amounts of lean tissue compared to athletes consuming 1.2 g/kg, despite both groups performing identical resistance workouts.

