- **Increasing Frequency Without Lowering Per-Session Volume**: Deciding to train chest 3x per week and doing 10 sets in each session (30 sets/week), immediately blowing past MRV into severe overtraining.
- **Thinking More Frequency Is Always Better**: Moving to 4x or 5x per week frequency for large muscle groups creates persistent low-grade connective tissue inflammation and never allows complete SRA recovery.
- **Ignoring Synergistic Overlap**: Counting tricep volume only as direct cable pushdowns while ignoring the 8 sets of heavy bench press performed earlier in the week.

### How to Measure Progress
- **Average Load Maintenance Across Sets**: You should be able to maintain your target load within 1 to 2 reps across all prescribed sets in a workout.
- **Absence of Chronic Joint Soreness**: High-quality volume distribution eliminates the deep joint and tendon aching that typically follows 15-set single-muscle marathons.

