### Introduction
In the pursuit of lean muscle mass, some lifters reduce dietary fat to extreme lows, hoping to maximize their carbohydrate budget. This is a dangerous physiological miscalculation. Dietary fats are not merely high-density energy sources (9 kcal/gram); they are active signaling molecules, vital structural components of all cellular membranes, and the **obligate chemical precursors for steroid hormone synthesis, including testosterone**. Chronically suppressing dietary fat impairs your endocrine profile and halts muscle growth.

### Learning Objectives
- Explain the biochemical pathway linking dietary cholesterol to testosterone synthesis.
- Establish the minimum dietary fat intake floor (0.8 to 1.2 g/kg/day) to safeguard hormonal health.
- Distinguish between saturated, monounsaturated (MUFA), and polyunsaturated (PUFA) fatty acids.
