1. **Purchase a Digital Gram Scale**: Measure all foods in grams, not cups, spoons, or subjective estimates. A "tablespoon" of peanut butter can easily vary from 15g to 35g (100 to 220 kcal).
2. **Execute a 2x/Week Meal Prep Habit**: Cook proteins (chicken, beef) and starches (rice, potatoes) in bulk twice a week (e.g., Sunday and Wednesday evening) and store in airtight glass containers.
3. **Apply the 14-Day Calibration Rule**:
