### Introduction
Lifting weights in the gym provides the stimulus; recovery outside the gym produces the adaptation. No amount of protein shakes, creatine, or advanced training programming can compensate for chronic sleep deprivation. During sleep, your body orchestrates an intricate hormonal cascade that repairs micro-tears in myofibrils, clears adenosine from brain tissue, and replenishes intramuscular glycogen stores.

### Learning Objectives
- Understand the 4 stages of human sleep architecture and their specific roles in physical and neural recovery.
- Quantify the hormonal impact of sleep duration on testosterone, growth hormone, cortisol, and insulin sensitivity.
