### Introduction
The scale is simultaneously one of the most useful and most psychologically misleading tools in fitness. In a muscle-building phase, seeing the scale climb can trigger anxiety about fat gain; seeing it stay flat can trigger frustration about wasted effort. Natural muscle growth is a slow, gradual biological process. To know with absolute scientific certainty that your caloric surplus is building dense skeletal muscle rather than unwanted visceral and subcutaneous fat, you must implement a **Multi-Point Body Composition Tracking Matrix**.

