### Introduction
One of the most paralyzing dilemmas for fitness novices is deciding whether to focus on losing fat or gaining muscle first. A person who looks thin in oversized clothing but carries noticeable adiposity around the midsection when unclothed often fears that cutting calories will make them look emaciated, yet fears that eating more will make them fat.

