When body fat is excessively high (above 22-25% in men, above 32-35% in women), systemic low-grade inflammation and reduced insulin sensitivity in skeletal muscle impair muscle protein synthesis. Excess calories in this state are preferentially partitioned into adipocytes. Conversely, when body fat is very low (under 10-12% in men, under 20-22% in women), the body's internal energy reserves are minimal, necessitating an external energy surplus to sustain optimal anabolic signaling.

