### Introduction
The single greatest cause of failure among beginner lifters is not bad programming or poor exercise selection—it is unrealistic expectations. Modern social media feeds display fitness influencers who claim to have built 12 kilograms of shredded muscle in three months while shedding fat.

When an honest beginner follows a disciplined program for six weeks, gains 1.2 kg of muscle, and notices their lower abdomen has not transformed into a six-pack, they conclude that their genetics are broken and quit. Understanding the biological ceiling of human muscular hypertrophy inoculates you against discouragement, allowing you to execute your transformation with clarity and quiet confidence.

### Learning Objectives
