### Introduction
The modern fitness industry is saturated with routines designed for advanced competitive bodybuilders: 6-day Push/Pull/Legs splits, 5-day body-part splits ("chest day", "arm day"), and high-volume marathons. When an untrained beginner attempts to follow a 6-day split, the outcome is predictable: extreme muscle soreness, inadequate recovery, central nervous system burnout, and eventual abandonment within a month.

For the novice lifter, the **3-Day Full Body Blueprint** is physiologically superior in every measurable category. It maximizes the frequency of muscle protein synthesis, manages systemic fatigue, fits seamlessly into a busy schedule, and produces faster strength and aesthetic gains than any other split architecture.

### Learning Objectives
- Understand the physiological reasons why high-frequency, moderate-volume full-body training outperforms low-frequency splits for beginners.
- Master the alternating Workout A / Workout B training architecture.
