- Execute an exact 12-week beginner full-body routine with exercises, sets, and rep targets.

### Detailed Explanation
To understand why full body works so effectively for beginners, consider the math of muscle stimulation:
- **Bro-Split (1x per week)**: You hit chest once on Monday with 16 sets. Muscle Protein Synthesis is elevated for 48 hours. By Wednesday evening, MPS returns to baseline. For the remaining 5 days of the week, your chest does not grow. Over a year, your chest receives **52 growth stimuli**.
- **Full-Body Split (3x per week)**: You hit chest with 3 to 4 high-quality sets on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday. Each session triggers a 48-hour MPS wave. Your chest remains in a near-continuous state of anabolic remodeling throughout the entire week. Over a year, your chest receives **156 growth stimuli** with virtually zero wasted "junk volume."

\`\`\`
THE 3-DAY ALTERNATING SCHEDULE
Week 1: Monday [Workout A] │ Wednesday [Workout B] │ Friday [Workout A]
Week 2: Monday [Workout B] │ Wednesday [Workout A] │ Friday [Workout B]
(Alternates continuously across the 12-week mesocycle)
\`\`\`

Between each training day sits a mandatory 48-hour recovery window (Tuesday, Thursday, Weekend). This allows the central nervous system, joints, and muscular glycogen reserves to fully restore, ensuring every session is attacked with maximum intensity and focus.

### Scientific Background
