### Introduction
The fitness culture of the late 20th century popularized the concept of the "bulking season." Bodybuilders would consume 4,000 to 5,000 calories a day—eating pizzas, mass-gainer shakes, and endless plates of pasta—gaining 15 to 20 kg over the winter, only to spend four grueling months dieting off the fat before summer.

For a beginner or skinny-fat individual, this approach is disastrous. Rapid weight gain promotes **adipocyte hyperplasia** (the creation of brand new fat cells, which can never be eliminated without surgery, only shrunk). Furthermore, carrying excess visceral fat impairs insulin sensitivity, meaning future excess calories are partitioned preferentially into fat rather than muscle. This lesson teaches you the art of the **Lean Anabolic Surplus**: fueling muscle growth with mathematical precision while keeping body fat tightly managed.

### Learning Objectives
- Calculate a precise lean surplus (+150 to +250 kcal) tailored to your metabolic rate.
- Set realistic weekly and monthly rate-of-weight-gain targets.
- Identify the biological signs of nutrient spillover (excess fat gain).
