### Detailed Explanation
Every gram of each macronutrient provides a specific quantity of metabolizable energy:
- **Protein**: 4 kcal per gram (Tissue construction, enzymatic processes, TEF)
- **Carbohydrates**: 4 kcal per gram (Primary fuel for high-intensity muscular work)
- **Dietary Fat**: 9 kcal per gram (Hormonal synthesis, cellular membranes, organ insulation)

\`\`\`
MACRONUTRIENT ALLOCATION HIERARCHY
Step 1: Set Protein     -> 1.8 to 2.2 g / kg of bodyweight
Step 2: Set Dietary Fat -> 0.8 to 1.2 g / kg of bodyweight (20-30% of total calories)
Step 3: Set Carbohydrates -> Allocate ALL remaining calories to carbohydrates
