There is no object in modern fitness that causes more unnecessary despair, premature program-hopping, and emotional devastation than the ordinary bathroom scale. A beginner wakes up on Tuesday, steps on the scale, sees a number that is 1.2 kg higher than yesterday, and enters an immediate spiral of panic: *"My diet failed! I gained 1.2 kg of fat overnight!"*

