### Scientific Background: The Fitness-Fatigue Model
Developed by Dr. Vladimir Zatsiorsky, the **Fitness-Fatigue Model** explains that every training session produces two opposing biological after-effects:
1. **Fitness (Adaptation)**: A long-lasting, slow-decaying increase in physical capacity (myofibrillar hypertrophy, motor unit recruitment).
2. **Fatigue**: A short-lasting, fast-decaying state of systemic, neural, and connective tissue fatigue.

$$\\text{Preparedness (Gym Performance)} = \\text{Fitness} - \\text{Fatigue}$$

When you train hard for 6 to 8 consecutive weeks, fatigue accumulates in the central nervous system, joints, and muscular tendons. Eventually, the magnitude of accumulated fatigue matches your fitness gains, masking your true capacity. You feel weak not because you haven't built muscle, but because **fatigue is masking your fitness**. 

\`\`\`
THE FITNESS-FATIGUE DYNAMICS
Session Completed ──► Fitness Increases (Slow decay, long-term)
                  └──► Fatigue Accumulates (Fast decay, masks fitness)
Net Performance = Fitness MINUS Fatigue
A Deload eliminates the fatigue spike, allowing underlying fitness to express itself!
