### Step-by-Step Implementation
1. **Audit Your Current Numbers**: Review your latest training log and calculate your current relative strength ratio for each of the 5 movement patterns (Load Lifted in kg / Bodyweight in kg).
2. **Identify Your Primary Weak Link**: Most skinny-fat lifters are severely deficient in the **Hinge** and **Vertical Pull** patterns (posterior chain weakness from desk sitting).
3. **Set 16-Week Benchmark Targets**: Choose one Level 2 benchmark for each pattern and program progressive overload systematically toward that milestone.
4. **Transition to Micro-Loading When Progression Slows**: When moving from novice to intermediate, you will no longer add reps every single workout. Expect progression to occur over 2 to 3-week cycles; celebrate adding 1 rep or 1 kg.

### Common Mistakes
- **Testing 1-Rep Maxes Constantly**: Grinding out ugly, dangerous 1-rep maximums every Friday. High-rep testing (e.g., 8 to 10 reps with strict form) provides a vastly safer and more accurate measure of hypertrophy-linked strength than risky 1RMs.
- **Sacrificing Range of Motion for Load**: Reaching an "intermediate milestone" by performing half-squats or bouncing dumbbells off the chest. A repetition only counts if it passes through the full anatomical range of motion under complete eccentric control.
- **Ignoring the Pull-to-Push Balance**: Reaching an intermediate bench press while being unable to perform 5 strict pull-ups or rows. This creates structural shoulder imbalance, leading to subacromial impingement and rounded posture.

