### Introduction
Congratulations: you have spent the last 6 to 9 months executing progressive overload, hitting your protein targets, mastering movement mechanics, and transforming your body composition. Your waist has shrunk, your shoulders have widened, your core is dense, and your relative strength has doubled.

You have officially graduated from the "skinny-fat beginner" category. However, as you advance into intermediate territory, the law of diminishing returns begins to apply to pure body recomposition. Simultaneous fat loss and muscle gain becomes slower and harder as your body approaches its genetic baseline. To continue making continuous progress over years 2, 3, and beyond, you must learn how to transition into **Dedicated, Phased Training Mesocycles**.

